{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2sJrVNEioKokqn6msy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because `related()` in `src/app.py` stores similarity scores as Python floats, and the DynamoDB serializer rejects floats. The log shows `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `similar` was `[]`, so no float was written. From the second publish on, each story has at least one related story with a float score. The handler's catch-all turns the `TypeError` into the 500.\n\n**Fix:** `related()` now stores each score as `Decimal(str(score))`, so no float reaches `put_item`.\n\n**Prevention:** I added a test that publishes three stories in a row, which the existing test never did. The in-memory fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so the test fails if a float comes back. Both tests pass with `python3 -m unittest discover tests`.\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":24279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906},"output_tokens":310,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28cf0044-7f0a-4eae-8f02-3bad242e781c","uuid":"6acd13e4-3a35-4267-88df-fac7a09858c9","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:29:16.407Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2sJbrpmgYqakUqRE1q"}
